  "text": "BRANCH ANALYSIS: feat/caddy-tailscale-migration-from-tws\n\nKey findings:\n1. The branch attempted to migrate from socat + SSH tunneling to Caddy + Tailscale\n2. Commits show a clear progression of adding Caddy/Tailscale, then removing socat/SSH code\n3. However, the CURRENT STATE is INCOMPLETE/INCONSISTENT:\n   - Caddy/Tailscale references were DELETED from docker-compose.yml and scripts\n   - Port mappings revert to HAProxy-only approach (lines 55-61 of docker-compose.yml show HAProxy)\n   - Dockerfile added HAProxy config template BUT also shows old SSH_TUNNEL variables still in docker-compose\n   - Design docs were created then DELETED from the branch\n\n4. Current working state:\n   - socat IS removed (good)\n   - SSH tunneling code IS removed (good)\n   - Caddy/Tailscale installation code IS in Dockerfile (good)\n   - BUT port_forwarding() uses HAProxy instead of Caddy (line 140-142 in common.sh)\n   - Tailscale/Caddy env vars are in docker-compose but not used\n   - No start_tailscale() or start_caddy() functions are called from run.sh\n\n5. This looks like an ABANDONED/ROLLED-BACK effort to migrate to Caddy+Tailscale, replaced by HAProxy approach instead\n\n6. 21 commits total, all from 2025-11-07 (today)",
